From 1506c673535c5f66a982318de5a493c47f0011d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 00:16:59 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(skills): mirror stage-transition envelope + surface real
 helper failures

Address CodeRabbit review on #279:
- Fallback `forge comment` bodies now mirror the exact structured envelope
  `beads-context.sh stage-transition` emits (Stage:/Summary:/Decisions:/
  Artifacts:/Next:, multi-line) instead of a pipe-joined single line, so the
  transition record parses consistently whether written via the helper or the
  kernel-native fallback. (plan/dev/validate/ship/review)
- Stage-transition + context-validate steps no longer mask real helper
  failures: `[ -f ] && cmd || true` and `... || forge issue show` become
  if/else that skip ONLY when the helper is absent; a present-helper failure
  stays visible.
- dep-guard Step 5c: store-contracts failures are no longer swallowed and
  non-contract exits are no longer mislabeled "No contracts found"; only the
  genuinely-advisory check-ripple degrades gracefully, so a kernel-native
  setup is still never hard-blocked.
- Regenerated the committed .codex/skills mirror (skills-sync drift 0).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
